WEBVTT

00:06.510 --> 00:10.740
<i>I'm still proud of it.</i>

00:11.120 --> 00:12.490
Of course! It'd be my pleasure!

00:12.950 --> 00:15.990
<i>The fact that I was able 
to answer right away.</i>

00:17.230 --> 00:17.990
<i>Even now.</i>

00:20.100 --> 00:21.190
<i>To this day...</i>

00:34.160 --> 00:36.440
Did I fall asleep?

01:23.560 --> 01:32.320
TONIKAWA

01:23.560 --> 01:32.320
TONIKAWA

02:13.520 --> 02:17.530
<b>Episode 10     Thank You</b>

02:13.820 --> 02:18.360
If stargazing is what you really want to do, 
we don't need to go into the mountains.

02:18.880 --> 02:22.990
Uh... Oh, you mean the camping 
trip with Tokiko-san?

02:23.250 --> 02:26.060
The mountains are swarming 
with bugs in summer, you know.

02:26.060 --> 02:27.830
You'll get eaten alive.

02:28.550 --> 02:33.050
I wouldn't even consider 
going if you weren't.

02:34.090 --> 02:39.330
Yeah, but won't it be better to go up 
somewhere high to look at the night sky?

02:39.330 --> 02:45.020
For the record, there are places in 
the city where you can do just that.

02:45.650 --> 02:47.600
A certain building in Shibuya, for instance!

02:47.600 --> 02:51.930
It has an open roof that offers 
a wonderful view of the stars!

02:51.930 --> 02:57.650
There's also grassy turf, along with beds 
and hammocks for couples to cuddle on!

02:57.650 --> 03:00.800
See?! You can go stargazing 
without going into the mountains,

03:00.800 --> 03:02.160
and without the bugs, even!

03:02.630 --> 03:05.560
Well, that sounds like 
a great idea for a date.

03:06.090 --> 03:07.660
Fair enough...

03:08.000 --> 03:10.800
I just don't get what her deal is.

03:10.800 --> 03:12.540
Were the flyers really necessary?

03:12.540 --> 03:17.090
<b>Come have fun</b>

03:12.540 --> 03:17.090
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:12.540 --> 03:17.090
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:12.800 --> 03:16.340
What even is an "outdoor home party"?

03:17.090 --> 03:17.130
<b>Come have fun</b>

03:17.090 --> 03:17.130
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.090 --> 03:17.130
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.130 --> 03:17.170
<b>Come have fun</b>

03:17.130 --> 03:17.170
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.130 --> 03:17.170
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.170 --> 03:17.210
<b>Come have fun</b>

03:17.300 --> 03:17.340
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.300 --> 03:17.340
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.340 --> 03:17.380
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.340 --> 03:17.380
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.380 --> 03:17.420
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.380 --> 03:17.420
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.420 --> 03:17.460
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.420 --> 03:17.460
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.460 --> 03:17.500
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.460 --> 03:17.500
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.500 --> 03:19.550
<b>The more the merrier!</b>

03:17.500 --> 03:19.550
<b>Outdoor Home Party</b>

03:17.620 --> 03:19.550
An "outdoor home party"...

03:19.990 --> 03:21.800
Sounds good! Let's go!

03:22.090 --> 03:23.760
Wow, that was fast.

03:23.760 --> 03:27.400
I figured since you're an e-famous shut-in, 
you wouldn't be interested in camping.

03:27.400 --> 03:31.060
Don't try to make me into 
some icon of the indoors.

03:31.060 --> 03:33.690
Everyone knows camping is 
synonymous with solid *****!

03:33.690 --> 03:36.500
Wait, what? I thought you 
were gonna say "snake."

03:36.500 --> 03:39.440
I don't actually get what it means,
 but it's fun to say.

03:39.750 --> 03:41.150
Anarcho Cups!

03:41.150 --> 03:42.820
Are we allowed to say that?!

03:43.120 --> 03:45.370
It's camping jargon, and I 
have no idea what it means.

03:45.370 --> 03:47.120
I just wanted to say it!

03:47.120 --> 03:48.580
You're really cutting it close.

03:48.940 --> 03:53.690
As I've demonstrated, camping has a 
kind of appeal that is quite seductive.

03:54.250 --> 03:58.590
Think of how many people watch camping 
videos online to avoid reality!

03:58.590 --> 04:00.810
I know all about how great that can be!

04:00.810 --> 04:04.590
So now all that's left is to go! To go and 
really enjoy that appeal to its fullest!

04:04.820 --> 04:08.600
And there you have it. So is it cool 
if my sister and I come along?

04:08.960 --> 04:11.110
Okay. I'll let her know.

04:11.110 --> 04:14.170
Is it okay that we don't 
have a clue what to do?

04:14.170 --> 04:15.980
That shouldn't be a problem.

04:16.460 --> 04:19.960
If you're not sure about setting up a tent,
 there will be glamping amenities, too.

04:19.960 --> 04:23.990
You mean that setup that's 
fancy like a hotel?

04:24.330 --> 04:27.430
Yep. You can make the trip by car, 
and sleep in a bed if you want.

04:27.430 --> 04:30.100
That sounds super awesome!

04:30.100 --> 04:33.760
It sure does. It almost 
sounds too good to be true!

04:33.760 --> 04:34.990
It's fine.

04:34.990 --> 04:38.640
Tokiko owns the property and 
everything on it, anyway.

04:38.640 --> 04:40.220
Wait, she does?

04:40.220 --> 04:40.880
Yeah.

04:41.370 --> 04:45.410
She bought it specifically for 
stargazing back in the day,

04:45.410 --> 04:48.510
but figured it would be a waste to leave it 
as-is, so she turned it into a campground.

04:48.730 --> 04:50.030
She did?

04:50.030 --> 04:51.640
That's pretty impressive!

04:52.040 --> 04:54.940
Well, since she owned it already...

04:54.940 --> 04:57.150
I guess it'd be a waste not to use it.

04:57.470 --> 04:59.650
Then I wanna go, too!

05:00.000 --> 05:01.240
Kyuuma-chan?

05:01.240 --> 05:02.560
Good to see you again.

05:02.560 --> 05:03.780
See, my thing is...

05:03.780 --> 05:07.410
Despite appearances, I've always 
thought camping sounded fun!

05:07.650 --> 05:08.800
Despite what appearance?

05:08.800 --> 05:11.710
Easy, now. Kyuuma-chan's just dumb.

05:11.710 --> 05:13.830
My dad always used to tell me,

05:13.830 --> 05:17.420
"Kyuuma, if someone makes you cry,
 head up to the mountains!"

05:17.420 --> 05:20.420
<b>Menacing</b>

05:17.740 --> 05:20.420
"Your old man will make sure 
they stay buried there!"

05:20.800 --> 05:22.730
That's how camping works, right?

05:22.730 --> 05:24.320
Not at all, no.

05:24.320 --> 05:27.520
It sounds like your camping party would 
shrink a little with every outing.

05:27.520 --> 05:30.830
Kyuuma-chan, remember that anime 
about camping from a while back?

05:30.830 --> 05:31.990
It's like that.

05:31.990 --> 05:34.400
Oh, yeah! <i>Laid-Back Ca</i>—

05:35.660 --> 05:40.190
Wait, that's what camping's like?! 
I wanna go! I wanna go bad!

05:40.190 --> 05:42.750
What exactly did she think it was before?

05:40.190 --> 05:44.590
Take me, take me, take me, take me!

05:42.750 --> 05:45.600
Easy, now. Kyuuma-chan's just dumb.

05:45.600 --> 05:48.900
If we're taking a whole group, 
I'll invite Ginga-kun and the others.

05:48.900 --> 05:50.820
Oh, that sounds good.

05:52.200 --> 05:54.430
You're gonna bury bodies in the hills?!

05:54.430 --> 05:55.830
No, no...

05:55.830 --> 05:58.160
I'm inviting you on a camping trip!

05:58.160 --> 05:59.830
Oh, camping!

06:00.590 --> 06:07.970
I gotta ask, bro, is that lady 
from the other day gonna be there?

06:08.270 --> 06:10.610
The lady from the other day?

06:11.020 --> 06:14.000
Oh, you mean Aya-san?

06:14.000 --> 06:14.600
Yeah.

06:15.340 --> 06:18.160
I figure, considering what happened,

06:18.160 --> 06:20.230
I've gotta settle up with her.

06:20.470 --> 06:22.730
I-I see...

06:23.220 --> 06:27.240
<i>What does he even mean? Whatever it is,
 I hope it's just rom-com stuff.</i>

06:30.820 --> 06:35.030
Are you going to attend this 
outdoor home party thing, Chitose?

06:35.030 --> 06:39.210
As a fan of Saito Takao-sensei's 
<i>Survival</i>, of course I am.

06:39.210 --> 06:40.510
Wait, <i>that's</i> why?

06:40.510 --> 06:42.580
Was that really a camping manga, though?

06:43.010 --> 06:48.070
There's also the fact that Nee-sama's husband 
looks like he has no clue about camping,

06:48.070 --> 06:51.090
so it'll be a great chance to teach him 
how harsh Mother Nature can be!

06:52.370 --> 06:55.470
Chitose-chan, have you ever 
been camping before yourself?

06:55.960 --> 07:00.330
I've learned everything there is to know 
about it from Saito Takao-sensei's <i>Survival</i>.

07:00.330 --> 07:01.870
Oh, this bodes poorly.

07:01.870 --> 07:05.340
I'll teach that idiot just 
how scary rats can be!

07:05.340 --> 07:07.730
Pretty sure we won't be running into rats...

07:08.290 --> 07:11.020
You think it'd be okay if we came along?

07:11.020 --> 07:14.800
Aren't we going to be accompanying 
Chitose-chan anyway?

07:14.800 --> 07:19.760
But if we're working, that means we can't 
exactly take part in any dinners or drinking...

07:21.280 --> 07:23.140
Eh, I'm sure it'll be fine.

07:23.140 --> 07:25.000
Yeah, you're probably right.

07:25.700 --> 07:29.040
It looks like we'll be camping 
with quite a big group.

07:29.040 --> 07:32.140
Looks that way. And Chitose's 
gang will be coming, too.

07:32.410 --> 07:35.520
Family and friends all assembling together...

07:35.520 --> 07:37.310
That makes it feel like a big deal.

07:37.310 --> 07:40.770
I'm looking forward to it. It'll almost
 be like a wedding reception.

07:40.770 --> 07:43.940
When you put it that way, 
I suddenly feel embarrassed...

07:43.940 --> 07:45.430
Huh? Really?

07:45.430 --> 07:49.480
Well, I would be happy about having 
our marriage celebrated.

07:49.480 --> 07:52.880
I bet even the stars above 
will give us their blessing!

07:52.880 --> 07:55.470
There you go being romantic again.

07:58.530 --> 08:00.540
I'm so excited for this camping trip!

08:00.540 --> 08:01.300
Yeah.

08:01.300 --> 08:02.710
I agree!

08:02.710 --> 08:08.090
<b>Campground</b>

08:02.710 --> 08:08.090
<b>Car</b>

08:03.100 --> 08:08.090
Now, as I mentioned earlier, there are two 
routes that take us to our destination.

08:08.090 --> 08:13.340
<b>Campground</b>

08:08.420 --> 08:13.340
One will escort us directly to 
the campground via a vehicle.

08:13.340 --> 08:17.350
<b>Campground</b>

08:13.340 --> 08:17.350
<b>Car</b>

08:13.610 --> 08:17.350
The other involves hiking from the foot 
of the mountain to our destination.

08:17.750 --> 08:21.650
The hike is estimated to take 
around four hours, incidentally.

08:21.650 --> 08:23.100
So, which will it be?

08:23.360 --> 08:25.310
Do you even have to ask? Obviously—

08:25.310 --> 08:26.360
I wanna hike!

08:27.280 --> 08:29.110
H-Hang on a sec, darling!

08:29.520 --> 08:31.930
Are you serious about a four-hour
 hike in the mountains?

08:31.930 --> 08:34.030
I mean, we're going camping!

08:34.030 --> 08:37.320
The whole point is to feel the 
breath of the wild, right?

08:37.320 --> 08:38.620
Tsukasa-sama.

08:38.620 --> 08:39.990
What should I put you down for?

08:41.300 --> 08:44.240
I-I'll be hiking, then...

08:44.240 --> 08:45.370
Very good.

08:45.640 --> 08:50.000
She doesn't want to walk, but she
 does want to stick with Senpai!

08:50.910 --> 08:53.430
Is it all right if I take the car, though?

08:53.430 --> 08:55.470
I need to finish some work before we leave.

08:55.470 --> 08:59.170
Understood. I'll be back 
later to collect you.

08:59.170 --> 09:00.260
Okay!

09:00.260 --> 09:03.020
Let's climb us a mountain!

09:03.490 --> 09:05.040
Yeah!

09:05.040 --> 09:06.440
Yeah...

09:12.120 --> 09:15.070
Climbing mountains... is really hard!

09:16.010 --> 09:18.440
You never miss a cue, do you?

09:18.440 --> 09:21.460
H-How many kilometers do we have left?

09:21.460 --> 09:23.430
That's a weird question to ask.

09:23.430 --> 09:26.120
We've only been walking for twenty minutes.

09:26.120 --> 09:31.010
I notice that Kyuuma girl 
hasn't been following us at all.

09:31.010 --> 09:32.540
Is she gonna be okay?

09:33.640 --> 09:36.140
Whoa, she's so far behind...

09:36.140 --> 09:37.780
Want me to nab her?

09:38.360 --> 09:42.940
You all can keep going. I'll bring her along.

09:43.620 --> 09:44.660
Tsukasa-chan—

09:44.660 --> 09:46.970
Damn, she's fast.

09:46.970 --> 09:49.400
Almost like a ninja...

09:49.700 --> 09:52.150
Well, we'd better keep on moving.

09:52.150 --> 09:53.400
Roger!

09:56.960 --> 09:58.160
What's up?

09:58.160 --> 10:00.460
Hey, Paisen's wife!

10:00.930 --> 10:03.980
I was just wondering what this flower is.

10:03.980 --> 10:07.110
Oh, this is cape jasmine.

10:07.110 --> 10:08.040
Cape jasmine?

10:08.520 --> 10:11.100
It bears a fruit called "sanshishi."

10:11.100 --> 10:14.550
In the old days it was used to 
treat bleeding and inflammation.

10:14.790 --> 10:16.320
What's inflammation?

10:16.320 --> 10:18.550
Basically, when something 
is swollen or bruised.

10:18.840 --> 10:23.560
You make a poultice out of ground sanshishi, 
egg yolk, and buckwheat, then slap it on.

10:23.830 --> 10:26.110
Really? And that actually works?

10:26.110 --> 10:29.090
Well, probably not as 
well as modern medicine.

10:29.090 --> 10:32.550
Anyway, we need to get walking 
or we won't be able to catch up.

10:32.550 --> 10:34.070
Huh? O-Oh, you're right!

10:34.660 --> 10:38.070
Still, this is a lot of fun. 
I've never seen most of this stuff!

10:38.300 --> 10:41.780
Really? I've seen all of it before.

10:43.080 --> 10:45.500
Wow! What a cute mushroom!

10:45.500 --> 10:46.580
Is it a matsutake?

10:46.580 --> 10:47.850
Don't touch it.

10:48.340 --> 10:49.220
Why?

10:49.220 --> 10:52.450
That's amanita virosa. 
Eat it and you're dead.

10:53.210 --> 10:55.630
There are poison mushrooms in Japan?!

10:55.630 --> 10:57.840
They grow all over the world.

10:57.840 --> 11:03.050
<b>Amanita virosa</b>

10:57.840 --> 11:08.730
<b>Amanita virgineoides</b>

10:57.840 --> 11:08.730
<b>Stubble rosegill</b>

10:58.210 --> 11:00.980
As a general rule, if you find a 
white mushroom in the mountains,

11:00.090 --> 11:08.730
<b>False parasol</b>

11:00.510 --> 11:08.730
<b>Clitocybe connata</b>

11:00.980 --> 11:03.220
you should absolutely not eat it.

11:03.220 --> 11:06.160
There's an edible type 
called stubble rosegill,

11:06.160 --> 11:08.730
but you're better off assuming 
they're all poisonous.

11:10.700 --> 11:13.750
I'm never gonna eat enoki again...

11:13.750 --> 11:15.860
That's not the issue.

11:16.110 --> 11:18.790
Anything sold in a grocery store is fine!

11:18.790 --> 11:21.860
I'm talking about the stuff 
growing in the mountains.

11:23.250 --> 11:27.340
And we're never going to catch up at 
this rate, so let's take a shortcut.

11:31.260 --> 11:33.600
I hope Tsukasa-chan and 
Kyuuma-chan will be okay.

11:33.600 --> 11:37.850
I hear you. These mountain trails can 
be rough. It might be hard to catch up.

11:37.850 --> 11:40.260
I wouldn't worry if I were you.

11:40.570 --> 11:42.040
Wha... Chitose-chan?

11:42.040 --> 11:44.260
You were taking so long, 
I came to see what was up.

11:44.870 --> 11:48.570
You really have no idea who 
you're dealing with, do you?

11:48.570 --> 11:52.520
It'd take a lot more than a mountain trail 
to give Nee-sama any kind of trouble.

11:52.520 --> 11:56.620
Wow, we actually made it!

11:56.620 --> 12:00.530
See? The trail can be steep, but if you 
know what you're doing, you can manage.

12:02.150 --> 12:05.060
We should be able to sit down soon.
 Then we'll take a break.

12:05.060 --> 12:06.640
You sure?

12:06.640 --> 12:09.600
I thought you wanted to catch 
up with Paisen and the others.

12:09.600 --> 12:10.790
No worries there.

12:12.310 --> 12:13.540
We just did.

12:13.920 --> 12:15.390
Huh? Tsukasa-chan?!

12:15.880 --> 12:16.770
No way!

12:16.770 --> 12:18.680
When did you catch up?

12:18.680 --> 12:21.310
Wouldn't be much of a ninja if 
I couldn't handle mountaineering.

12:21.310 --> 12:23.340
You're actually a ninja?!

12:23.340 --> 12:25.300
Verily she nin-nin is!

12:25.680 --> 12:29.430
Okay, okay, the path still 
continues for a while.

12:29.430 --> 12:30.560
Let's get going.

12:30.880 --> 12:34.810
See what I mean? She's got 
stronger legs than most.

12:34.810 --> 12:36.320
Y-Yeah...

12:37.420 --> 12:40.950
Tsukasa-chan, you don't actually 
like climbing mountains, right?

12:40.950 --> 12:46.130
Of course not. It makes me want to point out 
people invented cars and trains for a reason.

12:46.130 --> 12:49.590
But you seem really good at making 
your way through the mountains.

12:49.590 --> 12:52.080
Well, compared to you, darling.

12:52.560 --> 12:55.230
Y'know, Tsukasa-chan... 
I think you're a tsundere.

12:55.230 --> 12:56.960
That's not what this is!

12:57.540 --> 12:58.480
Are you mad?

12:58.480 --> 12:59.940
I am not.

13:03.310 --> 13:08.860
<i>She told me that she'd go out 
with me if I married her.</i>

13:09.970 --> 13:13.480
<i>And I replied instantly: 
"Of course! It'd be my pleasure!"</i>

13:14.070 --> 13:16.480
<i>I lost consciousness right after that,</i>

13:16.480 --> 13:18.980
<i>so I don't remember the rest very clearly...</i>

13:19.670 --> 13:25.020
<i>But I get the feeling that, right before 
I passed out, she was smiling.</i>

13:26.190 --> 13:28.110
Good morning, darling.

13:28.610 --> 13:29.970
Did you sleep well?

13:31.760 --> 13:34.700
Tsukasa-chan? Wait... Where are we?

13:34.990 --> 13:37.790
The campground. Are you still half-asleep?

13:38.240 --> 13:42.550
Oh, right. I was so exhausted from 
walking, I wanted to rest a little...

13:42.550 --> 13:45.490
You were only asleep for about ten minutes.

13:45.490 --> 13:48.720
Really? It felt a lot longer.

13:49.370 --> 13:52.470
I have to say, it really 
is quiet here in the woods.

13:52.470 --> 13:54.420
The weather's nice, too.

13:55.900 --> 13:58.730
Are we pretty far from the others?

13:59.040 --> 14:02.090
I think so. I don't hear their voices.

14:02.090 --> 14:04.260
I see...

14:05.470 --> 14:06.030
Well, then—

14:06.030 --> 14:07.860
Hang on. "Well, then" what?

14:09.350 --> 14:12.610
I mean... we might as well.

14:12.610 --> 14:14.370
Might as well what, exactly?!

14:14.810 --> 14:19.460
It's just... kind of embarrassing 
to get into real specifics,

14:19.460 --> 14:23.410
but let's just say I'd like to 
kiss you while no one is looking.

14:23.410 --> 14:25.760
That was pretty damn specific, 
if I'm being honest.

14:26.110 --> 14:26.930
You don't want to?

14:27.610 --> 14:29.340
It's not that...

14:29.340 --> 14:32.330
But I'd be embarrassed if anyone saw us.

14:32.330 --> 14:33.330
I see.

14:33.330 --> 14:34.680
Right?

14:34.680 --> 14:37.460
I personally wouldn't be embarrassed, though.

14:37.460 --> 14:39.390
Could you maybe try to be?!

14:39.750 --> 14:42.650
Oh, who cares if you make out a little?

14:42.910 --> 14:44.790
It's not like it hurts anyone.

14:44.790 --> 14:48.050
People like you showing up is 
why I'm in no hurry to start!

14:48.050 --> 14:50.530
Come on, it's fine. You're already married.

14:50.530 --> 14:52.660
Physical intimacy is crucial.

14:52.940 --> 14:55.850
Nasa-kun wants to smooch, doesn't he?

14:55.850 --> 14:56.980
Yes, of course.

14:56.980 --> 14:58.790
Don't humor her!

15:00.020 --> 15:02.920
I have to say, this campground is really nice.

15:02.920 --> 15:06.800
Thank you. Hearing that 
makes the trip worthwhile.

15:07.180 --> 15:11.090
Y'know, I bought this property because 
the view of the stars is just lovely.

15:11.090 --> 15:12.020
Really?

15:12.020 --> 15:12.680
Oh, yes.

15:13.420 --> 15:17.430
As if the moon is right within arm's reach.

15:17.430 --> 15:20.710
I see. Tonight should be really special, then.

15:20.710 --> 15:23.440
Yes, you're in for quite a treat.

15:23.870 --> 15:28.440
She'll probably loosen up a bit once 
it gets dark, too, so hang in there.

15:28.440 --> 15:29.430
Sure!

15:29.430 --> 15:31.200
Would you buzz off already?!

15:31.840 --> 15:33.220
Sure, sure.

15:33.220 --> 15:37.490
By the way, I've prepared a 
glamping tent for you two,

15:37.490 --> 15:39.450
so that's where you'll be staying tonight.

15:40.040 --> 15:43.020
I'm sure your wife is sick to 
death of the old-fashioned kind.

15:43.020 --> 15:44.960
Sounds good! Thank you.

15:48.060 --> 15:50.950
She really is generous, isn't she?

15:51.780 --> 15:55.310
Come to think of it, she told me 
something interesting the other day.

15:55.310 --> 15:56.100
What's that?

15:56.430 --> 15:59.260
About how spouses have a special relationship.

16:00.010 --> 16:04.100
And Chitose-chan asked me something 
about why we got married.

16:04.760 --> 16:09.100
Sometimes I think about that sort of thing...

16:10.320 --> 16:12.740
Am I special to you, darling?

16:13.090 --> 16:16.740
You are. You're one of a 
kind for me, Tsukasa-chan.

16:16.980 --> 16:18.990
I-I see...

16:20.160 --> 16:21.180
Of course.

16:22.480 --> 16:26.560
I guess we should head over to where 
the others are playing in the river.

16:30.860 --> 16:34.630
Why don't we go for a little walk? 
Just the two of us.

16:35.880 --> 16:37.910
Okay... Let's do that.

16:41.470 --> 16:44.550
It sure is quiet out here.

16:44.550 --> 16:45.740
Sure is.

16:50.900 --> 16:52.230
Kyuuma-chan!

16:53.280 --> 16:56.730
That's Ginga-kun and the others down there.

16:56.730 --> 16:59.410
Chitose's gang is with them, too.

16:59.850 --> 17:03.200
That's Kyuuma-chan and 
Aya-san who are swimming.

17:03.200 --> 17:06.790
With their clothes on, too. 
Did they think that through?

17:07.980 --> 17:10.160
Looks like everyone's accounted for, huh?

17:10.160 --> 17:12.800
Yeah, I guess so.

17:16.230 --> 17:18.070
Let's head over there for a bit.

17:18.070 --> 17:19.330
Y-Yeah.

17:23.590 --> 17:26.200
There's a beautiful stream up here, too!

17:26.200 --> 17:27.190
Seriously!

17:27.780 --> 17:29.420
You wanna wade in it?

17:30.320 --> 17:33.190
I'm wearing this long skirt, 
though, so it'd get wet.

17:34.610 --> 17:36.450
Allow me, then.

17:38.320 --> 17:40.430
I can hold it up so it won't get wet.

17:40.430 --> 17:43.950
H-Hey... I can't really walk like this.

17:44.580 --> 17:46.050
It's okay.

17:46.050 --> 17:48.300
I'll make sure you don't fall.

17:48.300 --> 17:49.810
You sure?

17:50.290 --> 17:54.230
It's hard to move at all, honestly.

17:54.230 --> 17:56.470
That works out nicely.

17:57.760 --> 17:59.000
C-Come on!

17:59.000 --> 18:01.550
D-Don't nibble my ear!

18:02.220 --> 18:04.190
Your ears taste good, Tsukasa-chan.

18:04.190 --> 18:08.070
S-Stop! Your breath is... It tickles!

18:08.070 --> 18:09.180
I love you.

18:10.140 --> 18:12.140
Aw, come on!

18:14.440 --> 18:16.490
Wait, Kyuuma-chan's gone?

18:16.880 --> 18:17.770
You think she's...

18:17.770 --> 18:18.980
Stranded?

18:18.980 --> 18:21.440
No, that's not likely.

18:21.440 --> 18:22.740
We're off the trail now,

18:22.740 --> 18:27.080
and these campgrounds are big, 
but they're surrounded by a fence,

18:22.740 --> 18:30.460
<b>Camera</b>

18:22.740 --> 18:30.460
<b>Entrance</b>

18:22.830 --> 18:30.460
<b>Camera</b>

18:27.080 --> 18:29.440
on top of being monitored with cameras.

18:29.440 --> 18:32.130
So it's impossible to be stranded 
if she's on the grounds.

18:32.480 --> 18:34.240
So she's just lost?

18:34.240 --> 18:35.160
Most likely.

18:35.160 --> 18:38.210
Well, we still need to find her.
It's almost time for dinner,

18:38.210 --> 18:40.390
so let's search for her first.

18:46.470 --> 18:47.390
Huh?

18:48.020 --> 18:49.390
Well...

18:49.440 --> 18:54.150
<b>Lost</b>

18:49.870 --> 18:51.290
<i>This isn't good at all!</i>

18:51.290 --> 18:53.750
<i>Everyone except me got lost somehow!</i>

18:54.150 --> 18:55.970
What a mess.

18:55.970 --> 19:00.250
Now I'm going to have to 
find every single one of them!

19:00.250 --> 19:03.660
For now, I should head back 
to where we all were...

19:05.940 --> 19:07.950
Where even am I?!

19:07.950 --> 19:12.080
She said it was impossible to get stranded, 
but it's possible! It's super possible!

19:12.080 --> 19:13.670
Because of how freaking huge it is!

19:14.240 --> 19:18.670
Oh, man, what do I do? I mean, I'm feeling 
really exhausted, and my legs hurt...

19:21.010 --> 19:23.930
<i>F-For now, let's lie down and think.</i>

19:24.710 --> 19:26.420
<i>Calm yourself...</i>

19:34.790 --> 19:37.190
What? My darling isn't back yet?

19:37.620 --> 19:41.220
Is this one of those "the hunter 
becomes the prey" situations?

19:41.220 --> 19:43.530
Yeah, that about sums it up.

19:43.530 --> 19:48.740
I know this place is big, but it's 
not exactly easy to get lost in.

19:48.740 --> 19:51.210
Well, he's pretty indoorsy.

19:51.210 --> 19:54.710
Jeez, that Paisen is a real handful, huh?

19:55.790 --> 19:57.760
And where have you been, Kyuuma-chan?

19:57.760 --> 19:58.710
Potty!

19:59.610 --> 20:00.880
I... see.

20:00.880 --> 20:01.760
Yep!

20:05.120 --> 20:06.350
<i>I had a dream.</i>

20:07.220 --> 20:08.720
<i>A dream of that day.</i>

20:09.720 --> 20:13.230
<i>The day when I met her for the first time.</i>

20:14.530 --> 20:16.230
<i>Why did she ask me that?</i>

20:16.450 --> 20:17.330
Darling?

20:17.330 --> 20:20.070
<i>What did she really mean?</i>

20:18.400 --> 20:19.580
Darling...

20:20.910 --> 20:26.240
Darling, if you sleep out here, 
the bugs will eat you alive.

20:26.990 --> 20:29.240
Huh? Tsukasa-chan?

20:29.830 --> 20:32.160
Did I fall asleep?

20:32.160 --> 20:34.100
Yep. Out like a light.

20:34.100 --> 20:35.930
Wait, it's really dark!

20:36.480 --> 20:38.060
And did Kyuuma-chan turn up?

20:38.060 --> 20:39.750
Yes, a long time ago.

20:40.040 --> 20:41.650
Oh, that's good.

20:41.650 --> 20:43.890
Come on, we should get going.

20:43.890 --> 20:45.780
They're going to start the barbecue.

20:46.750 --> 20:48.500
<i>Come to think of it, yeah...</i>

20:48.500 --> 20:53.730
<i>When she was leaving on that night, 
I called out, desperate to stop her.</i>

20:55.220 --> 20:56.710
Hey, Tsukasa-chan.

20:57.550 --> 21:01.280
On that day, you said you'd go 
out with me if I married you.

21:01.280 --> 21:02.700
What did you mean by that?

21:03.280 --> 21:04.940
Did I never tell you?

21:05.680 --> 21:06.910
N-No, you didn't!

21:08.070 --> 21:09.530
I didn't?

21:10.630 --> 21:13.700
Well, in that case, 
I don't think I'll tell you.

21:14.410 --> 21:17.040
Aw, that's mean!

21:17.340 --> 21:20.280
I mean, do you really not know?

21:21.570 --> 21:24.300
Because of, "What? Why?"

21:25.350 --> 21:30.770
If most people got those kind of conditions 
from a girl they barely knew,

21:30.770 --> 21:32.110
they'd ask, "What? Why?"

21:32.110 --> 21:34.180
At best, they'd be confused or just silent.

21:34.660 --> 21:39.060
If nothing else, I really doubt there's 
anyone else who'd be able to respond instantly.

21:39.590 --> 21:42.800
Suspicion. Doubt. Distrust.

21:43.250 --> 21:46.750
Humans can talk about love all day long,

21:46.750 --> 21:49.580
but it's never quite clear 
how much they really trust.

21:50.080 --> 21:54.250
Sometimes, no amount of words 
can make them trust someone.

21:54.250 --> 21:56.080
A degree of doubt is always there.

21:56.910 --> 22:00.400
So when they hear something 
strange, they always ask,

22:00.400 --> 22:02.220
"What? Why?"

22:02.690 --> 22:05.140
Because they don't trust 
who they're talking to.

22:05.140 --> 22:08.090
But you answered, and right away, at that.

22:08.750 --> 22:10.940
"Of course! It'd be my pleasure!"

22:12.080 --> 22:15.350
That proves you didn't doubt me.

22:16.450 --> 22:20.770
When I wasn't sure about you, 
you took a leap of faith for me.

22:21.310 --> 22:25.860
B-But... what if I said it was 
just because I was infatuated?

22:26.180 --> 22:27.520
That'd be fine, too.

22:28.120 --> 22:31.020
Even if you were being silly 
or not thinking it through,

22:31.020 --> 22:33.490
there'd come a moment when 
the truth would shine through.

22:34.240 --> 22:37.510
You know how they say that,
with surprise proposals,

22:37.510 --> 22:40.880
the face gives the answer away 
before the words come out?

22:41.130 --> 22:42.570
Y-Yeah...

22:42.570 --> 22:44.130
It's like that.

22:44.600 --> 22:47.460
You can find the answer inside of an instant.

22:49.200 --> 22:54.510
I fell in love with you because you 
were willing to trust me first.

22:55.770 --> 22:58.630
You trusted me,

22:58.630 --> 23:01.200
so I decided to trust you.

23:02.040 --> 23:03.900
Thank you, Nasa-kun.

23:05.520 --> 23:09.520
<i>Tsukasa-chan, the reason I was able 
to answer you so quickly that night</i>

23:09.520 --> 23:13.910
<i>was because I was overjoyed 
that you turned my way.</i>

23:14.600 --> 23:17.230
<i>I was just so, so happy...</i>

23:17.780 --> 23:23.220
<i>And that's why I'll always 
be proud of my answer.</i>

23:24.920 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

23:25.800 --> 23:29.800
Big Bro Nasa! I'll make sure to take 
down anyone who gets in your way!

23:29.800 --> 23:31.550
Just the sentiment is enough, Ginga-kun!

23:31.550 --> 23:33.370
Yes, sir! I'll cool my heels!

23:33.370 --> 23:35.250
He really never calms down, does he?

23:35.250 --> 23:38.180
He's a good kid! He just idolizes 
certain problematic figures...

23:38.180 --> 23:39.930
I'm not sure how that's "good" at all.
